course: dictionary
lesson: 2488
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Deadly» can mean able to kill, but it can also mean very great or complete, as in «deadly serious». Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Some wild mushrooms are deadly poisonous, so we must never eat ones we pick ourselves.» The words poisonous and eat are clues. Here deadly means able to kill, so swap in «able to kill» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The mosquito biting your arm is, for people, the deadliest animal of all.» Deadliest is the strongest form of deadly, just as bigger is stronger than big. Deadly, deadlier and deadliest all come from the same word.
explain: «Poinsettias are not deadly; eating them may cause a mild tummy upset.» The word not tells you the writer is saying these plants are not able to kill. Read the whole sentence, not just the one hard word.
fact: Deadly is an adjective, and it can also be an adverb: «deadly serious» means very serious.
fact: «Deadly» can mean able to kill or very likely to cause death, such as a deadly snake or a deadly poison.
fact: «Deadly» can also mean very great or complete, as in «deadly quiet».
fact: Never touch or eat something you do not know. Tell an adult straight away.
fact: In Australian slang, «deadly» can mean excellent or awesome, especially in Aboriginal English.
exercise: «Some wild mushrooms are deadly poisonous, so we must never eat ones we pick ourselves.» What does deadly mean here? | *Able to kill | Excellent and awesome | Very accurate in a game | Very quiet
exercise: «The room fell into deadly silence when the teacher walked in.» What does deadly mean here? | *Very great or complete | Dangerous to touch | Able to kill | Very accurate in a game
exercise: «The mosquito biting your arm is, for people, the deadliest animal of all.» Find and copy the word that is the strongest form of deadly. | *deadliest | mosquito | animal | biting
test: «A deadly snake can be very dangerous.» What does deadly mean in «a deadly snake»? | Very quiet | Very accurate | *Able to kill | Excellent
test: Jayden says «deadly serious» means dangerous. What does it really mean? | Very accurate in a game | Dangerous to touch | Able to kill | *Very serious
exam: «Poinsettias are not deadly; eating them may cause a mild tummy upset.» What does this sentence tell you? | Poinsettias are deadly and must never be touched | *Deadly means able to kill, and poinsettias are not that dangerous | Deadly means excellent | Poinsettias are a kind of mushroom
